      "evidence": "The Statement gives the admissible-label sum without restricting n, and also includes m₀(d)=1 when d=1 and 0 otherwise. For the empty tree there are no internal edges or vertices, so the literal labeling rule admits the unique empty labeling, with empty product 1 for every d; if the empty tree has no root, the sum is instead undefined. Either way, the formula does not yield m₀(d)=0 for a nonunit simple d unless an n≥1 restriction or an explicit empty-tree convention is added.",
